<!--
    The status-bar icon. The same mark as ic_yadlo, at 24dp and inset.

    It has to be a flat silhouette: Android discards every colour in a notification small icon and
    re-tints what is left by alpha, so a multi-colour vector arrives as a white blob. The mark was
    already a single filled path, which is the only reason this is a copy rather than a redraw.

    Lives in the shared module rather than in androidApp because the receiver that references it
    does too, and a resource looked up across that boundary would have to go through
    getIdentifier() and a string.
-->
